.TH DAQ-SSH-CHECK.SH 1 "2026-10-28" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools 1.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
daq-ssh-check.sh \- check Kerberos and the ssh paths to the Mu2e DAQ hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B daq-ssh-check.sh
[\fB\-H\fR \fI"host ..."\fR]
[\fB\-F\fR \fIssh_config\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fIseconds\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR]
[\fB\-P\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBClient side.\fR Run this on your own laptop or workstation after
.BR install\-ssh\-config.sh (1),
or whenever ssh to the DAQ stops working. It prints one PASS or FAIL
line per check, in this order:
.IP 1. 4
\fBKerberos.\fR A valid ticket exists, and its default principal equals
\fBMU2EDAQ_KRB5_PRINCIPAL\fR when that is set (the installer records it).
On macOS a second \fBkinit\fR silently makes another principal the
default; the FAIL line then suggests the \fBkswitch\fR command that
restores yours.
.IP 2. 4
\fBResolved settings.\fR For each host, \fBssh \-G\fR must give
\fBGSSAPIAuthentication yes\fR. MC-2 and MC-1 control-room hosts must
jump through \fImu2egateway0*\fR, MC-1 workers through
\fIg2gateway0*\fR, and a gateway must not resolve to your local login
name (the sign that \fI~/.ssh/config_mu2e\fR is not included). No
network traffic.
.IP 3. 4
\fBLive login.\fR \fBssh \-o BatchMode=yes\fR to each host runs
\fBid \-un\fR and \fBhostname\fR. A "Permission denied" usually means
your principal is not in that account's \fI.k5login\fR.
.IP 4. 4
\fBnoVNC portal\fR (with \fB\-P\fR). On \fImu2e\-mgr\-01\fR,
\fBhttps://localhost/\fR must answer 200.
.PP
Hosts are checked in the order given, so list a gateway before the
hosts behind it.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then .env file, then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-hosts " " \fI"H1 H2 ..."\fR
Hosts to check. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_SSH_CHECK_HOSTS\fR. Default:
\fI"mu2egateway01.fnal.gov mu2e\-mgr\-01.fnal.gov"\fR.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
ssh configuration file to evaluate, passed to \fBssh \-F\fR.
Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_SSH_CONFIG\fR. Default: ssh's own.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " " \fISEC\fR
ssh \fBConnectTimeout\fR for the live checks. Environment:
\fBMU2EDAQ_SSH_CHECK_TIMEOUT\fR. Default: 15.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-static
Run steps 1 and 2 only.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-portal
Also run step 4.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_KRB5_PRINCIPAL
Principal the active ticket should belong to; written by
.BR install\-ssh\-config.sh (1)
to \fI~/.mu2edaq/env\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every check passed, 1 when any failed, 2 on a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
scripts/daq\-ssh\-check.sh                 # ticket, settings, logins
scripts/daq\-ssh\-check.sh \-P              # plus the noVNC portal
scripts/daq\-ssh\-check.sh \-s \-H mu2e\-dl\-01.fnal.gov
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR install\-ssh\-config.sh (1),
.BR start\-novnc\-connection.sh (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR kswitch (1)
